    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied because scripts could not be run. Present risk is dominated by a TC1 path from untrusted public issues to broad private-repo reads and irreversible public PR egress. The only declared preventive control is a per-tool approval prompt, but because arguments are collapsed and users approve many calls per session, it is scored as a summary-style approval gate and cannot reduce residual below high on these paths. Forecast rises to critical if that gate decays further under model upgrade, autonomy increase, or control removal. Missing structural controls that would materially reduce risk are least-privilege credential scoping, raw-action approval review, and MCP definition pinning/identity verification."
  },
